    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Intake + Validation\nWebhook `POST /lead-intake` receives `{name, email, company, message, source}`.\n\n`Validate Input` checks required fields + email format. Invalid payloads never reach enrichment - they get an immediate **400** with a `details` array of the specific problems (fail-fast input validation at the system boundary).",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "note-intake",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1620,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Idempotency / Dedupe\n`leadId` is a deterministic hash of the lowercased email - the same lead always gets the same ID, submission after submission.\n\n`If Row Exists` / `If Row Not Exists` (n8n-nodes-base.dataTable, operation `rowExists`/`rowNotExists`) run in parallel against `lead_crm`, filtered on `email`. A duplicate short-circuits straight to a 200 response (`routed: \"duplicate\"`) with the existing score - no re-scoring, no duplicate row, no wasted LLM call.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "note-dedupe",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Dedupe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -940,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich + Score (LLM)\nDomain is derived deterministically in code. Company-size/industry classification and the 1-100 sales-readiness score (with reasoning) come from a single structured-JSON call to `OpenRouter Chat Model` (anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5) via a Basic LLM Chain + Structured Output Parser - one round trip, not two, to keep the webhook response fast.\n\n`retryOnFail` (3 tries, fixed 2s wait) covers transient LLM/network failures. Note: n8n's node-level retry is fixed-interval, not true exponential backoff - documented honestly in docs/01-lead-capture-crm.md.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "note-enrich",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Enrich",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Route + Adapters\nScore >= 70 -> `Adapter: Hot Lead Alert` (demo sink: Data Table `lead_notifications`, 1-node swap to Slack) fires first, then both paths converge on `Adapter: CRM Upsert` (demo sink: Data Table `lead_crm`, 1-node swap to a real CRM).\n\nBoth adapters are separate sub-workflows called via Execute Workflow, each with its own `errorWorkflow` pointing at `[CORE] Error Handler` and its own `retryOnFail`.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "note-route",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Route",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const msg = $json.error || $json.message || 'Unknown node failure';\nreturn [{ json: { nodeError: String(msg) } }];"
      },
