    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "throw new Error('Lead pipeline node failure (caller already received 502): ' + ($json.nodeError || 'unknown'));"
      },
      "id": "code-rethrow-for-error-handler",
      "name": "Rethrow For Error Handler",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        380,
        900
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Failure Contract (fixed)\nWith `responseMode: responseNode`, a node that hard-fails before any Respond node runs leaves the caller with an HTTP 200 and an EMPTY body - silent failure, easy to misread as success. (Found by the workflow-02 builder testing their own pipeline; confirmed here too via this workflow's own forced-failure test, execution 14.)\n\nFix: every node with a realistic external-failure mode (`onError: continueErrorOutput`) now routes its error output here instead of hard-failing the execution. `Handle Node Failure` extracts the message, `Respond 502` gives the caller a real non-2xx status with a details field, then `Rethrow For Error Handler` re-throws so the OVERALL execution still ends in `error` status and `[CORE] Error Handler` still logs a `core_error_log` row - callers get an honest error AND the fleet-wide error log still catches it.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "note-failure-contract",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Failure Contract",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        780
      ]
    }
  ],
